{"id":"gotcha-example-001","type":"gotcha","fact":"Example: Truthy check on numeric values fails for explicit zero - if (value) is false when value === 0.","recommendation":"Use !== undefined or !== null instead of truthy checks when the value could legitimately be 0 or empty string.","confidence":"high","provenance":[{"source":"coderabbit","reference":"PR review","date":"2026-01-09"}],"tags":["javascript","type-coercion","validation"],"affectedFiles":["**/*.ts"],"affectedServices":[],"createdAt":"2026-01-09T00:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-01-09T00:00:00Z","usageCount":0,"helpfulCount":0,"outdatedReports":0}
{"id":"gotcha-redact-compose-order-001","type":"gotcha","fact":"Internal.Redact.redactErr composes paths-first: redactSshStderr . redactIPv4 . redactHostname . redactPathText. Putting path-redaction LAST causes the hostname matcher to consume path segments containing dots (e.g. '/var/log/app.example/x' renders as '<host>' instead of '<path>'). Discovered by QuickCheck during WU2.","recommendation":"Keep redactPathText as the LEFT-MOST (innermost) substitution in any redactor pipeline. Add a QuickCheck property that a path containing a dot survives the full pipeline as <path>, not as <host>.","confidence":"high","provenance":[{"source":"feat/terminal-backends-design","reference":"WU2 redactor implementation","date":"2026-05-14"}],"tags":["security","redaction","quickcheck"],"affectedFiles":["src/PureClaw/Internal/Redact.hs","test/Internal/RedactSpec.hs"],"affectedServices":[],"createdAt":"2026-05-14T00:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-05-14T00:00:00Z","usageCount":0,"helpfulCount":0,"outdatedReports":0}
{"id":"gotcha-replace-all-prefix-001","type":"gotcha","fact":"A global replace_all of a shorter prefix run AFTER renaming a longer prefix that contains it will corrupt the already-renamed text. E.g. renaming pto_ -> _pto_ then to_ -> _to_ turns _pto_* into _p_to_*. Spec-document field-name migrations got mangled this way during plan-review iter 3.","recommendation":"When migrating field-name prefixes, sequence longest-prefix renames LAST (or use word-boundary regex). Verify with a 'grep -rn <new_prefix>' after each rename. Doc edits with shared substrings (e.g. _pto_ shares 'to_') are the highest-risk site.","confidence":"high","provenance":[{"source":"feat/terminal-backends-design","reference":"plan-review iter-3 doc fix","date":"2026-05-14"}],"tags":["editing","migration","tooling"],"affectedFiles":["docs/**/*.md"],"affectedServices":[],"createdAt":"2026-05-14T00:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-05-14T00:00:00Z","usageCount":0,"helpfulCount":0,"outdatedReports":0}
{"id":"gotcha-hpc-aarch64-darwin-001","type":"gotcha","fact":"On aarch64-darwin with GHC 9.12.3, 'cabal test --enable-coverage' fails at link time with missing __hpc_tickboxes_* symbols when the executable depends on a coverage-instrumented library. Reproducible on main with no PureClaw-side cause. CI on x86_64-linux succeeds with the same command.","recommendation":"Do NOT try to run the coverage gate locally on aarch64-darwin. Rely on CI (.github/workflows/ci.yml step 'Run tests with coverage') as the source of truth for the .coverage-thresholds.json gate. Plain 'cabal test' (no --enable-coverage) works locally.","confidence":"high","provenance":[{"source":"feat/terminal-backends-design","reference":"WU11 coverage gate attempt","date":"2026-05-14"}],"tags":["build","coverage","hpc","aarch64-darwin","ghc-9.12"],"affectedFiles":[".github/workflows/ci.yml",".coverage-thresholds.json"],"affectedServices":[],"createdAt":"2026-05-14T00:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-05-14T00:00:00Z","usageCount":0,"helpfulCount":0,"outdatedReports":0}
{"id":"gotcha-telegram-allowlist-conflation-001","type":"gotcha","fact":"Telegram receiveUpdate allows an update iff isAllowed policy (UserId userId) || isAllowed policy (UserId (show chatId)) — numeric user id OR chat id, both wrapped in the UserId newtype (intentional access-control conflation, like Signal wrapping phone+UUID). Usernames are NOT supported (from.username is not parsed). Unauthorized updates are consumed, logged at WARN, dropped, then receiveUpdate recurses; _tch_lastChat is updated ONLY after auth passes so a blocked sender cannot redirect replies.","recommendation":"Do not expect username-based allow-listing for Telegram; use numeric user/chat IDs. Preserve the update-lastChat-only-after-auth ordering.","confidence":"high","provenance":[{"source":"agent","reference":"PR #73","date":"2026-05-31"}],"tags":["gotcha","telegram","security"],"affectedFiles":["src/PureClaw/Channels/Telegram.hs"],"affectedServices":[],"createdAt":"2026-05-31T00:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-05-31T00:00:00Z","usageCount":0,"helpfulCount":0,"outdatedReports":0}
